      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add experimental Claw lifecycle diagnostics",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add an experimental core doctor check that projects the canonical Claw lifecycle status model into structured health findings\n- report partial installs, missing or modified agents, workspace drift, package drift/incomplete state, MCP ownership drift, unresolved cron ownership, and orphaned subordinate rows\n- preserve source MCP placeholders while inspecting runtime config so resolved credentials cannot create false drift\n- keep the check and ordered doctor contribution absent unless `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`\n\n## Contract\n\n- doctor reuses `claws status` ownership states instead of independently interpreting managed resources\n- absent and pre-Claws state produce no findings and no state directory, database, schema, migration, chmod, checkpoint, or journal-mode change\n- existing state is observed through one read-only handle; missing experimental ownership tables are treated as empty only in read-only mode\n- unreadable, invalid, or forward-version state databases return one structured error finding rather than aborting doctor\n- source MCP config is read through the canonical source-config API; `${ENV_VAR}` placeholders remain unexpanded\n- diagnostics are advisory and do not mutate config, files, scheduler state, provenance, database bytes, metadata, schema, or journal mode\n\n## Verification\n\n- test-source typecheck\n- focused Oxlint: 0 warnings and 0 errors\n- formatting and `git diff --check`\n- 183 focused lifecycle, collector, shared-state, core-check, and doctor-contribution tests\n- absent/pre-Claws tests prove doctor creates no state and changes no bytes\n- existing-state test compares database bytes, mtime, mode, `sqlite_master`, `user_version`, and `journal_mode` before and after doctor\n- invalid and newer-schema tests prove open failures become structured findings and handles close cleanly\n- full Codex review against #102406: no actionable findings\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27\n- Depends on: #102406 MCP ownership\n- This PR: read-only lifecycle and drift diagnostics\n- Next: #102959 uses the same ownership model for grouped update planning\n\nDoctor lands after every add/remove owner so it can reuse one authoritative status model instead of inventing partial resource checks. The Claws CLI and doctor surface remain gated by `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`.\n",
